Please see the Ardour website at https://ardour.org/ for all documentation.

For information on building Ardour:

https://ardour.org/development.html


Fork features
=============

This fork (https://github.com/TimotheeDvt/ardour) adds the following on top
of upstream Ardour:

Track folders
  - Group tracks into folders that can be collapsed/expanded (Alt+C).
  - Add tracks to an existing folder from the current selection, and
    "Remove from Folder" in the context menu.
  - Optional bus per folder; folder and bus rows are merged.
  - Folder color picker, with a color strip on member tracks.
  - Collapsed folders show plain rectangle ghosts of their member regions
    (also on the bus row); folded tracks are ignored when zooming to fit
    all tracks.
  - Folders appear in the mixer, with tabs.
  - Undo/redo support for folder operations.

Audio quantize
  - Quantize audio regions, with a strength setting and cancel support.

Region gain
  - Gain node inside the region to adjust the region gain directly.
  - "Normalize to -1dB" in the region context menu (gain node limited to
    the normalized level).

Master bus
  - Mute L / Mute R buttons.

Fixes
  - Export no longer crashes when the backend enlarges buffers during
    freewheel; large cycles are processed in chunks.
  - Plugins declaring bufsz:minBlockLength are supported; removed an assert
    on VST loading and a BBT offset assert.
  - Crash on non-MIDI event return, and on closing a session with folders.
  - Build fix for char8_t issue.
